.TH DCC-FAN-DAEMON 8 2026-11-22 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-fan-daemon \- fan control daemon of Dudes Control Center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-fan-daemon
.RB [ \-\-foreground | \-f ]
.RB [ \-\-debug | \-d ]
.RB [ \-\-help | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-fan-daemon
runs as root from
.BR dcc-fan-daemon.service .
Every 5 seconds it reads the CPU and GPU temperatures and sets both fans
through the embedded controller (EC), either along the active fan curve
(automatic mode) or to the fixed speed chosen in
.BR dcc-gui (1)
(manual mode).
Fan curves come from the desktop user's
.I profiles.json
(see
.BR dudes-control-center (7)).
.PP
When the
.BR dcc_fan (4)
kernel module is loaded, the daemon reaches the EC through it (and writes the
fan duty every 5 seconds for the module's watchdog); otherwise it uses the
I/O ports 0x62/0x66 directly.
The log names the method at start; STATUS reports it as
.BR EC_ACCESS=module | ports .
.PP
Clients connect to
.IR /run/dcc-fan.sock ;
only root and members of the group
.B dudes-control-center
are accepted (checked with SO_PEERCRED on every connection).
.SS Safety
.TP
.B Watchdog
The daemon reports to the systemd watchdog every 2 seconds.
If its main loop hangs for 30 seconds, systemd kills and restarts it.
.TP
.B Kernel watchdog
With
.BR dcc_fan (4)
loaded, the module itself sets the fans to 100\~% when the daemon has not
written for 30 seconds.
.TP
.B Stop fail-safe
Whenever the service stops (crash, watchdog, stop, update), its
.B ExecStopPost
sets the fans to 100\~% with
.BR "dcc-fan-cli \-\-set 100" .
.TP
.B Sensor failure
After 2 invalid CPU temperature readings in a row the fans run at 100\~%
until the sensor delivers valid values again.
.TP
.B Emergency temperature
At 95\~\(deC or more (CPU or GPU) the fans run at 100\~% in every mode until
the temperature drops below 90\~\(deC.
An emergency ends manual mode; control returns to the fan curve.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-foreground ", " \-f
Stay in the foreground (the service uses this).
.TP
.BR \-\-debug ", " \-d
Log every control step (temperatures, target and fan duty every 5 seconds);
by default only changes of mode, profile or safety state are logged.
The log level can also be changed at run time with
.BR "dcc-fan-cli \-\-log\-level" .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a short help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dcc-fan.sock
Command socket.
.TP
.I /var/log/dudes-control-center/FAN_DAEMON.log
Log (rotated at 1 MB, 5 old files kept).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/dcc-fan-daemon.service
Service; it does not start while
.I /etc/dudes-control-center/disabled-fan
exists.
.SH NOTES
Switching fan control off with
.BR dcc-component (8)
leaves the fans at 100\~% until the next reboot; no EC command is known that
hands them back to the firmware while the system runs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-fan-cli (1),
.BR dcc-gui (1),
.BR dcc-component (8),
.BR dcc_fan (4),
.BR systemd.service (5)
